# one long paragraph per file). Line-based diffing/rendering them on every
# change is expensive for git, CI, and the GitHub PR UI. Mark them as
# generated so diffs are collapsed by default and diff/blame computation is
# skipped, which speeds up checkouts, pushes, and PR page loads. They are
# also already stored with pure LF endings, so `-text` skips the redundant
# per-checkout/per-add line-ending renormalization scan that `text=auto`
# would otherwise still perform on their full (hundreds-of-KB) content.
